quran[22]{c,v,t}:
  54,28,Inform them that the water is to be shared between them. Every (share of the) drink will be attended (in equitable proportion).
  54,29,But they roused a companion of theirs. So he took (a sword) in (his) hand and hamstrung (the camel).
  54,30,Then how (terrible) were My punishment and My warnings!
  54,31,"Indeed, We sent upon them (only) one mighty blast, and they became like the dry sticks of the fence builder."
  54,32,"Certainly, We have made the Qur’an easy to remember (by simplifying its lessons). So, is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,33,"(Then,) the people of Lut (Lot) rejected the warnings."
  54,34,"We sent a storm of stone upon them except the family of Lut (Lot). We saved them (from the torment) at dawn,*"
  54,35,"as a blessing from Us. Thus, We reward those who give thanks."
  54,36,"He had already warned them of Our strike, but they disputed the warnings."
  54,37,"They even tried to turn him away from his (angel) guests (to snatch them from him). So We blinded their eyes, (saying:) ‘Taste My punishment and My warnings.’"
  54,38,"Indeed, an abiding punishment visited them early in the morning."
  54,39,(Then it was said to them:) ‘Taste My punishment and My warnings.’
  54,40,"Certainly, We have made the Qur’an easy to remember (by simplifying its lessons). So, is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,41,"Indeed, the warnings (also) came to the people of Pharaoh,"
  54,42,"who denied all Our signs. So, We seized them with the crushing grip of the All-Mighty, the Most-Powerful."
  54,43,"Are your disbelievers better than those (before), or is there an exemption for you in the scriptures?"
  54,44,Or do they say: ‘We (all) are a victorious confederate (to be dominant over the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him)’?
  54,45,"Soon, their united front will be defeated (in the battle of Badr), and they will turn (their) backs, fleeing."
  54,46,But the Hour is their appointed time. And the Hour will be most catastrophic and most bitter.
  54,47,"Indeed, the guilty are in error and madness."
  54,48,The Day they are dragged into the Fire upon their faces (they will be told:) ‘Taste the touch of Hell.’
  54,49,"Indeed, We have created everything according to a (precisely) programmed measure."
